<title>USA: N.J.'s United Healthcare System to close -- paper.</title>
<headline>N.J.'s United Healthcare System to close -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Healthcare System in Newark, N.J., will close as part of a $12 million takeover bid from Saint Barnabas Health Care System, Star-Ledger reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>About 560 of the current 1,200 employees might be offered jobs with Saint Barnabas, the newspaper said, adding that the shutdown could occur as early as Thursday.</p>
<p>The hospital, which is about $50 million in debt, is expected to file for bankruptcy Wednesday.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
</text>
